Overview
As the assigned Backend Developer for our Namibia Hockey Union group project, I was responsible for designing, implementing, and securing the backend infrastructure using Firebase. My role was to ensure seamless data handling, user management, and real-time functionality to support the core features of the mobile application.

Technologies & Services Used
•	Firebase Authentication – User login and registration
•	Cloud Firestore – NoSQL database for structured app data
•	Firebase Storage – Media file handling (e.g., profile images)
•	Firebase Security Rules – Role-based access control

Backend Functionality Implemented
1. User Authentication
•	Enabled secure user registration and login using Firebase Authentication.
•	Set up authentication state monitoring for seamless access control.
•	Implemented role-based tagging for different user types (e.g., Admins, Players, Coaches).
2. Database Design with Firestore
•	Designed a scalable Firestore schema with collections for:
o	users – storing role, profile info, and UID links
o	teams – storing team details and relationships to players
o	players – individual player registration and assignment
o	events – for tournament and match registration
•	Implemented real-time listeners to reflect live updates for team rosters and events.
3. Media Handling with Firebase Storage
•	Enabled upload of profile pictures and team logos.
•	Structured Storage paths to align with Firestore user and team IDs.
•	Applied storage rules to restrict access to authorized users only.
4. Security and Access Control
•	Wrote custom Firebase Security Rules to:
o	Allow only authenticated users to access sensitive data.
o	Restrict write permissions based on user roles.
o	Protect Storage and Firestore collections from unauthorized access.
Achievements
•	Successfully deployed a fully functional, real-time backend using Firebase services.
•	Ensured the app supports secure, role-based data access for multiple user types.
•	Contributed to a smooth, responsive experience by leveraging Firebase’s live syncing features.
•	Gained practical experience in NoSQL data structuring, Firebase rule-writing, and mobile backend integration.

Challenges & Solutions

Challenge	                                            Solution
Structuring dynamic relationships in Firestore	      Used subcollections and document references for relational modeling
Handling access control for multiple user roles	      Implemented and tested comprehensive Firebase security rules
Managing media uploads securely	                      Defined custom Storage rules and mapped files to authenticated user IDs

Conclusion
This backend development experience deepened my skills in cloud-based infrastructure and mobile app support. Firebase offered a versatile backend-as-a-service solution, and my contributions ensured that the Namibia Hockey Union app could scale securely and efficiently.

